-- title:
--   Special-fibre components are invertible ideal sheaves
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a package $\mathfrak X$ of data and properties for the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$ (properness, flatness, integrality and normality of `DRModel p` over the base, rational and geometric curve models together with their Galois and place compatibilities, cusp sections over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$, a distinguished smooth locus maximal among relatively smooth opens, and further fields, summarised here). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring that is a domain, with the hypothesis $h\varpi$ that its maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. Assume $H$, the conjunction of: finiteness of the node index type, the existence of oriented crossing charts, the étale-neighbourhood hypothesis [`V3Glue.Site.EtNbhd`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L99), injectivity of the map sending a node index to its point `xpt` of `XO p O`, closedness of each such point, and the hypothesis [`V3Glue.Site.ModelHyps p O`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L82). Assume further $h\xi$: each $\xi_j$ lies in the open `X0` of the chart input `C`, that is, differs from every marked node point. Then for every component index $v$, the ideal sheaf datum $\mathrm{comp}(v)$ on the glued scheme $Y$ is invertible: every point of $Y$ admits an affine open $U$ and $f \in \Gamma(Y,U)$ with the point in the basic open $D(f)$, such that the ideal cut out by $\mathrm{comp}(v)$ on the affine basic open of $f$ is generated by a single non-zero-divisor.
--
--   This is the assertion that the components of the special fibre of the glued resolution of $\mathfrak X \times_{\mathbb Z} \operatorname{Spec} O$, taken as vanishing ideal sheaves of the closures of their generic points, are effective Cartier divisors on that regular two-dimensional scheme. It is one of the ingredients verified at the site instance and consumed by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts), which assembles the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model together with its étale crossing charts.
